omapdrm/dispc: say why the runtime PM put failed

dispc_runtime_put() checks pm_runtime_put_sync() with a bare WARN_ON,
which reports that something went wrong and then discards the errno that
would say what.  It fired twice in a run of 1587 deliberate modesets on
the Pyra, both times from the atomic commit worker, and there was no way
to tell a device that merely declined to idle from a suspend callback
that actually failed.

Print the value.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/dss/dispc.c	2026-09-10 22:19:00.603565638 -0400
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/dss/dispc.c	2026-09-10 22:19:19.914758257 -0400
@@ -664,7 +664,14 @@
 	DSSDBG("dispc_runtime_put\n");
 
 	r = pm_runtime_put_sync(&dispc->pdev->dev);
-	WARN_ON(r < 0 && r != -ENOSYS);
+	/*
+	 * This fires, rarely, from the atomic commit worker.  A bare WARN_ON
+	 * throws away the one piece of information that would say why, so
+	 * print the errno: -EBUSY and -EAGAIN mean the device simply declined
+	 * to idle, anything else is a real failure of the suspend callback.
+	 */
+	WARN(r < 0 && r != -ENOSYS,
+	     "dispc_runtime_put: pm_runtime_put_sync returned %d\n", r);
 }
 
 static u32 dispc_mgr_get_vsync_irq(struct dispc_device *dispc,
